      "nets": ["UART_TX"],
      "observed": "The net named UART_TX includes J7 pins 1 and 2 and U5.26, and also includes the circuit's ground connections. Thus the UART transmit output and both of those header pins are grounded.",
      "expected": "J7.1 should be GND, J7.2 should be UART_TX, and J7.3 should be UART_RX; U5.26 should not be shorted to GND.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"55\") (name \"UART_TX\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"J7\") (pin \"1\") (pinfunction \"Pin_1\") (pintype \"passive\")) (node (ref \"J7\") (pin \"2\") (pinfunction \"Pin_2\") (pintype \"passive\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"26\") (pinfunction \"UART_TXD0\") (pintype \"bidirectional\"))"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J7.1→GND, pin2→`UART_TX` (SKW92A pin 26), pin3→`UART_RX` (SKW92A pin 25)"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The UART transmit signal is held at ground, preventing normal UART transmission; the debug header also has its first two pins shorted together at ground.",
      "confidence": 0.99
    },
    {
      "category": "open_connection",
      "components": ["J5", "U5"],
      "pins": ["J5.R1", "J5.R2", "J5.R3", "J5.R4", "J5.R5", "J5.R6", "U5.1", "U5.2", "U5.3", "U5.4"],
      "nets": ["unconnected-(J5-TD+-PadR1)", "unconnected-(J5-TD--PadR2)", "unconnected-(J5-RD+-PadR3)", "unconnected-(J5-TCT-PadR4)", "unconnected-(J5-RCT-PadR5)", "unconnected-(J5-RD--PadR6)", "LAN1_RX+", "LAN1_RX-", "LAN1_TX+", "LAN1_TX-"],
      "observed": "The RJ45 data and center-tap pins are unconnected. The corresponding module Ethernet pins are on separate nets containing only U5, so the jack is not connected to the module.",
      "expected": "For the specified Ethernet jack/interface to function, its data pairs must connect to the module's Ethernet port signals.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"75\") (name \"unconnected-(J5-TD+-PadR1)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"76\") (name \"unconnected-(J5-TD--PadR2)\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"16\") (name \"LAN1_RX+\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"1\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "netlist",
          "quote": "(net (code \"18\") (name \"LAN1_TX+\") (class \"Default\") (node (ref \"U5\") (pin \"3\")"
        },
        {
          "source": "spec",
          "quote": "J5 | RJ45 Amphenol RJMG1BD3B8K1ANR | Ethernet jack"
        }
      ],
      "impact": "The RJ45 connector cannot provide a wired Ethernet connection to the SKW92A in this design.",
      "confidence": 0.91
    }
  ],
  "summary": "The UART transmit path is definitively shorted to ground, contrary to the specified debug-header wiring. The RJ45 jack's Ethernet contacts are also left unconnected to the module, making the wired Ethernet interface inoperative."
}

